    "field": "Decadal climate variability",
    "problem": "There is little understanding of the causes and controls of abrupt climate regime changes, such as the significant 1976-77 shift in the North Pacific, prompting investigation into whether the atmosphere or ocean was the predominant driver of the event.",
    "method": "This study uses a hindcast simulation with an ocean general circulation model, forced by observed atmospheric heat fluxes and wind stresses, to simulate the 1976-77 Pacific climate shift and diagnose the physical oceanic processes that caused it.",
    "task": "The task is to use a sophisticated ocean model, forced by observed atmospheric data, to simulate and diagnose the causes of the abrupt 1976-77 climate shift observed in the North Pacific Ocean.",
